VDR Plugin 'vtsatip' Revision History
-------------------------------------

2026-10-24: Version 0.7.11
- The statistics page can be scrolled: its lines were not selectable, so the
  cursor and with it the page could not move, and the page went back to the top
  at every refresh. The lines are selectable now and the cursor stays on its
  line when the page is rebuilt.

2026-10-23: Version 0.7.10
- The RTP receive buffer is set with SO_RCVBUFFORCE if allowed (CAP_NET_ADMIN),
  the kernel cut it down to net.core.rmem_max (about 208 KiB) before. The size
  the socket really got is shown as rcvbuf= in SVDRP INFO and on the statistics
  page, a cut buffer is logged once. With RTP over TCP the kernel tunes the
  buffer of the connection (rcvbuf=auto), unless -r sets it.
- Pauses of 200 ms or more between two RTP packets are counted (pauses=) and
  logged with their relation to the last PLAY request; pauses up to 2 s after a
  PLAY request are counted separately (playpauses=), to find out whether the
  server stops the stream when the PIDs change.

2026-10-23: Version 0.7.9
- The default for releasing an unused stream is 30 seconds (was 20; the EPG
  scanner steps every 20 s, so a device in a scan pass was released and set up
  again at every step). A value stored in setup.conf stays.
- A device without a free frontend does not offer EPG scanning (ProvidesEIT()
  is false), so VDR does not drop transponders from its scan list that the
  device would have refused ("no SAT>IP server with a free frontend").
- README: a system without a number in -s CAPS counts as one frontend, with an
  example; EPG pause after scan.

2026-10-21: Version 0.7.8
- EPG scanning of the SAT>IP devices is automatic by default: they take part
  only if there is a kind of reception (sat, terrestrial, cable) provided by
  the servers that no other device (local DVB card) scans the EPG for. With the old default
  the EPG scanner took every free SAT>IP device, so a frontend of the server
  was busy all the time and was released and set up again about every 20
  seconds. "Enable EPG scanning" has the values automatic / no / yes now
  (setup.conf: -1 / 0 / 1; old stored values stay as they are). README section
  "EPG scan", which also explains how VDR's EPG scanner works (a step every
  20 s, scanning all the time unless EPGPauseAfterScan is set).
- EPG scanning can also be set per device ("VDR device N: EPG scanning",
  setup.conf EpgScanDevice0..n: -1 = as the general setting, 0 = no, 1 = yes).
- The release of an unused stream is logged at info level.

2026-10-21: Version 0.7.7
- Memory safety review (thanks to the reviewer on GitHub):
  - The device name (SVDRP LSTD, OSD) is read and written under a mutex; it
    was a cString reassigned while another thread could copy it.
  - The service ID lists of the CI slots are guarded, so saving the setup
    cannot disturb ProvidesChannel() running in another thread.
  - discoverM (UPnP) is guarded against SVDRP SCAN running while the setup
    switches discovery off.
  - ~cVtSatipDevice detaches all receivers and stops the device thread before
    it frees the buffers (VDR stops it only after the destructor).
  - RTSP waits can be aborted: deleting a tuner no longer waits for the
    timeouts of an unresponsive server (a forced thread cancel while the
    thread still uses the objects is avoided). The final TEARDOWN still waits.
- Tests: fake server mode "hang", concurrent SID list test.

2026-10-19: Version 0.7.6
- Stall watchdog: if a stream delivers no RTP for 5 seconds (10 seconds
  while waiting for the first packet after a tuning), the session is dropped
  and set up again. A server that stops sending without closing the RTSP
  session, or a TCP connection that died, used to leave a black picture until
  the channel was switched. New fake-server modes and tests (dead, deadstart,
  tcpdead).
- The ring buffers are emptied by the thread that reads them (GetData() and
  the section handler thread) instead of the tuner thread, as VDR's
  cRingBufferLinear requires.
- The channel name for INFO and the statistics is a copy guarded by a mutex;
  the "DVR open" flag is atomic.
- The size of the socket receive buffer is checked and a warning is logged
  (once) if the kernel limits it (net.core.rmem_max).
- Thanks to the reviewer of GitHub issue #1.

2026-10-19: Version 0.7.5
- Devices that are not used any more release their server frontend (TEARDOWN)
  after 20 seconds (-I, setup menu "Release unused stream after"). VDR only
  calls SetPowerSaveMode from the EPG scanner's pause, so streams used to stay
  open until VDR was stopped. Done in MainThreadHook, once a second.

2026-10-18: Version 0.7.4
- SVDRP INFO and the statistics page show the data rate and the longest pause
  between two RTP packets (now and since tuning), to find out whether video
  buffer underruns are caused by late delivery.

2026-10-17: Version 0.7.3
- DeviceType shows the delivery system of the current tuning (DVB-S2, DVB-S,
  DVB-T2, DVB-C ...) instead of "vtSAT>IP", so femon and scripts based on it
  show something useful. Also: GitHub Actions CI, tests/build_vdr.sh.

2026-10-16: Version 0.7.2
- UPnP: the device description is only fetched from the host that sent the
  announcement (LOCATION host must match the sender), with a test.
- README: limitations (S2X, C2 data slice, CI untested on hardware), security
  note. New file README.developer.

2026-10-16: Version 0.7.1
- Copyright and license notices in all files (GPL-2.0-only), derivation from
  the SAT>IP plugin and vtuner-ng marked, new file AUTHORS.

2026-10-15: Version 0.7.0
- Fixed server frontend per device in the setup menu.
- pids=all option (-a, setup menu): request the whole transponder.
- RTP packet counters (received, lost, reordered) in SVDRP INFO.
- Statistics page in the setup menu.
- README in English, translation check
  in the test suite.

2026-10-15: Version 0.6.0
- RTP over TCP (-T tcp, setup menu): RTP/RTCP interleaved into the RTSP
  connection ("$" frames), automatic fallback to UDP per server.

2026-10-15: Version 0.5.0
- Self-healing server compatibility: session IDs with leading zeros,
  servers without addpids/delpids, refused retune on a running session
  (new session), HTTP-like 503 -> the device moves to another server.
- Multicast transport (-T multicast / setup menu) with automatic unicast
  fallback per server.
- Satellite position filter per server (-s HOST|DVBS2-4:S19.2E,S13E).
- CI extension only on servers that have a CI (UPnP model detection, CI/NOCI).
- SVDRP ATTA/DETA, option -A (start detached).
- Service ID restriction per CI slot (-S).

2026-10-14: Version 0.4.0
- Setup menu (UPnP discovery mode, EPG scan, idle disconnect, CI slots and
  CA IDs, tracing, server list, red key = scan), settings kept in setup.conf
  and applied immediately, German translation, I18N rules in the Makefile.

2026-10-14: Version 0.3.0
- UPnP/SSDP discovery of SAT>IP servers (M-SEARCH, NOTIFY), description parsing
  without external libraries, several servers (-s can be repeated, -u),
  frontend accounting per server and delivery system, SVDRP SCAN.

2026-10-14: Version 0.2.0
- CI/CAM support through the SAT>IP x_pmt/x_ci extension (-c, -i, -Q),
  PMT PID detection from the PAT, PMT cache, session restart for servers
  that need x_pmt in SETUP.
- Test suite (tests/run_tests.sh) against a fake SAT>IP server.

2026-10-14: Version 0.1.2
- SETUP/PLAY query in the form vtuner-ng sends it (key order, fec and plts
  always for DVB-S/S2, default RTSP port left out of the URL).

2026-10-14: Version 0.1.0
- Initial version.
